{"strongs": "H1823", "word": "דְּמוּת", "translit": "de.mut", "root": "דמות", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "likeness, similitude", "definition": "דְּמוּת noun feminine likeness, similitude (mostly late) (according to Lag BN 12. 147 ff. mispunct. for דִּמְוַת from דִּמְוָה ; according to We Prol. 413. Eng. Tr. 389 an Aramaic Loan-word, but see Di Gen 5:1 , Dr JPh xi. 216 Che OP. 474 ) — absolute ׳ ד Isa 40:18 + 3 t.; construct ׳ ד Gen 5:1 + 16 t.; suffix דְּמוּתוֺ Gen 5:3 דְּמוּתֵנוּ Gen 1:26 — 1. likeness, similitude , of external appearance, chiefly in Ezek.: Ezek 1:5 ( likeness , i.e. something that appeared like) so v Ezek 1:26 ; Ezek 8:2 דְּמוּת כְּמַרְאֵה (אֵשׁׅ (compare Co ), Ezek 10:1 כִּסֵּא ׳ כְּמַרְאֵה ד ; compare also Dan 10:16 כִּדְמוּת בְּנֵי אָדָם i.e. one like the sons of man; similitude, resemblance Ezek 1:5 ; Ezek 1:10 ; Ezek 1:16 ; Ezek 1:22 ; Ezek 1:26 ; Ezek 10:10 ; Ezek 10:21 ; Ezek 10:22 דְּמוּת כְּמַרְאֵה אָדָם Ezek 1:26 ׳ מַרְאֵה ד ׳ כְּבוֺד י v Ezek 1:28 also 2Kgs 16:10 (pattern of altar), 2Chr 4:3 (images of oxen); of son in likeness of father Gen 5:3 ( P ); so also of man in likeness of God Gen 1:26 (|| צֶלֶם ) Gen 5:1 (both P ); compare Isa 40:18 what ׳ ד will ye compare to him ( אֵל ) ? || דִּמָּה q. v. 2. adverbially, in likeness of, like as Isa 13:4 compare Ezek 23:15 & ׳ כִּד Ps 58:5 . — Ezek 1:13 read וּבֵינוֺת , see בֵּין and J P Peters JBL 1892 40. 42 . On דְּמוּת אֶחָד Ezek 1:16 ; Ezek 10:10 (apparently masculine) compare Thes & Sm who translate the likeness of one had they all four ; Co reads אחת .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1962')\">BDB1962</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H1823')\">H1823</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1961')\">BDB1961</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1963')\">BDB1963</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>דְּמוּת</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>likeness, similitude</highlightword> (mostly late) (according to <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>BN 12. 147 ff.</sup></lookup> mispunct. for <bdbheb>דִּמְוַת</bdbheb> from <bdbheb>דִּמְוָה</bdbheb>; according to <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We<sup>Prol. 413. Eng. Tr. 389</sup></lookup> an Aramaic Loan-word, but see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup> <ref ref=\"Gen 5:1\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(1,5,1)\">Gen 5:1</ref>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr<sup>JPh xi. 216</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che<sup>OP. 474</sup></lookup>) — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 40:18\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(23,40,18)\">Isa 40:18</ref> + 3 t.; construct <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 5:1\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(1,5,1)\">Gen 5:1</ref> + 16 t.; suffix <bdbheb>דְּמוּתוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 5:3\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(1,5,3)\">Gen 5:3</ref> <bdbheb>דְּמוּתֵנוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 1:26\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(1,1,26)\">Gen 1:26</ref> — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>likeness, similitude</highlight>, of external appearance, chiefly in Ezek.: <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:5\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,5)\">Ezek 1:5</ref> (<highlight>likeness</highlight>, i.e. something that appeared like) so v<ref ref=\"Ezek 1:26\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,26)\">Ezek 1:26</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 8:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,8,2)\">Ezek 8:2</ref> <bdbheb>דְּמוּת כְּמַרְאֵה (אֵשׁׅ</bdbheb> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup>), <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:1\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,1)\">Ezek 10:1</ref> <bdbheb>כִּסֵּא</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כְּמַרְאֵה ד</bdbheb>; compare also <ref ref=\"Dan 10:16\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(27,10,16)\">Dan 10:16</ref> <bdbheb>כִּדְמוּת בְּנֵי אָדָם</bdbheb> i.e. <highlight>one like the sons of man; similitude, resemblance</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:5\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,5)\">Ezek 1:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,10)\">Ezek 1:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:16\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,16)\">Ezek 1:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:22\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,22)\">Ezek 1:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:26\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,26)\">Ezek 1:26</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,10)\">Ezek 10:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:21\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,21)\">Ezek 10:21</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:22\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,22)\">Ezek 10:22</ref> <bdbheb>דְּמוּת כְּמַרְאֵה אָדָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:26\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,26)\">Ezek 1:26</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מַרְאֵה ד</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כְּבוֺד י</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Ezek 1:28\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,28)\">Ezek 1:28</ref> also <ref ref=\"2Kgs 16:10\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(12,16,10)\">2Kgs 16:10</ref> (pattern of altar), <ref ref=\"2Chr 4:3\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(14,4,3)\">2Chr 4:3</ref> (images of oxen); of son in likeness of